Below are three coordinated patches to make the GeoTIFF loader honor both X and Y resolution (and thus non-square pixels) when it computes the tile “window” to read.  In outline:

1. Change `getResolution()` so it returns a two-element `[xRes, yRes]` array instead of a single scalar.
2. Store a two-element resolution factor (`[factorX, factorY]`) per source in `configure_()`.
3. Use both factors when computing the read “window” in `loadTile_()`.

Each patch is a *SEARCH/REPLACE* in `src/ol/source/GeoTIFF.js`.

